# Chaos module scope

All work happens in `modules/chaos`. Do not create, edit, delete, or commit files outside that directory.

Reading the core (headers, scripts, `modules/how_to_make_a_module.md`) is fine when you need an existing API. Changing it is not.

If a task cannot be done from inside the module, stop and ask before touching anything else.

## Where changes go

- C++: `modules/chaos/src/` (`Chaos_loader.cpp`, `Chaos_SC.cpp`, and new files next to them)
- Config: `modules/chaos/conf/`
- SQL: `modules/chaos/data/sql/db-auth/`, `db-characters/`, or `db-world/`

```text
❌ BAD  src/server/game/Entities/Player/Player.cpp
❌ BAD  data/sql/updates/pending_db_world/some_change.sql
✅ GOOD modules/chaos/src/Chaos_SC.cpp
✅ GOOD modules/chaos/data/sql/db-world/my_feature.sql
```

## When you need help

Look it up on the AzerothCore documentation index before inventing APIs, hooks, or SQL layout:

https://www.azerothcore.org/wiki/documentation-index

Use the page that matches the task (module creation, hooks, SmartAI, database). Do not guess a core function or hook that the docs or an existing module do not show.
